          "description": "Read-only dry run: runs the full optimisation in memory and reports, per image, the format Optiq would choose, bytes before and after, and the measured quality (SSIM, or pixel-exact). Writes nothing. Use it first to show the user the expected savings, then call optimize_images with the same arguments. ",
